/ActualText (zkBench: zkBench is the first open-source, generic, extensible, and configurable benchmarking framework designed for public-key cryptography and ZKPs. It offers extensible backends for benchmarking both low-level arithmetic operations and high-level ZKP circuits, using exemplary test vectors such as SHA-256 implementations in various ZKP tools or libraries. zkBench conducts comprehensive benchmarking of high-level ZKP circuits, covering execution time and memory consumption across the setup, proving, and verification phases. Additionally, it introduces a novel methodology that enables developers and researchers to perform detailed performance analysis of cryptographic algorithms and protocols. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
