/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (BabySpartan: Lasso-Based SNARK for Non-Uniform Computation: BabySpartan is an advancement in succinct non-interactive arguments of knowledge \(SNARKs\), merging SuperSpartan and Lasso protocols for Plonkish constraint systems. It focuses on improving computational efficiency by reducing cryptographic commitments to small values, addressing a challenge in SNARK technology deployment. Integrating SuperSpartan's framework with Lasso's commitment approach, BabySpartan aims to enhance the application of SNARKs in blockchain technologies. This development highlights a move towards specialized solutions within the blockchain industry, aiming to address technical challenges and expand blockchain capabilities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Binius: The Ulvetanna team's "Succinct Arguments over Towers of Binary Fields" introduces Binius, a novel SNARK construction approach using binary fields \(GF\(2\)\). This method aligns closely with digital circuit data types, significantly reducing memory and computational overhead. Binius features a polynomial commitment scheme for GF\(2\) with no embedding overhead and supports a range of binary field sizes.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
