/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Polygon ID's architecture integrates on-chain and off-chain elements alongside zero-knowledge proofs to construct a privacy-focused identity system. Its foundation lies in an identity state commitment on the blockchain, organized into three Merkle trees: the claims tree for individual claims storage, the revocations tree for logging invalidated claims, and the roots tree as a chronological record of identity states. This structure allows for claim retrieval, verification, and revocation. Claim interactions involve issuers adding claims with digital signatures to the claims tree, and users presenting these claims along with Merkle tree proofs to verifiers, who can ascertain the claim's validity and non-revocation status without exposing sensitive data. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
