/ActualText (ZK Email: a protocol that leverages DomainKeys Identified Mail \(DKIM\) signatures, which are cryptographic signatures attached to emails that verify the sender's domain, to enable users to prove they received an email from a specific sender. This method allows for the verification of off-chain data, such as email-based attestations, in a decentralized and privacy-preserving manner, leveraging ZKPs to maintain user anonymity while providing specific information.This can be effectively used to connect Web2 identities to onchain addresses. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
