297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (zkUniswap by Diego Estevez \(0xfuturistic\): zkUniswap is a conceptual fork of UniswapV3 utilizing a zkVM \(RISCZero\) for off-chain computation of swap steps. It processes swap requests made on-chain; a relay computes this off-chain, posting the output and proof back to the EVM. If validated, the swap executes. zkAMMs, like zkUniswap, integrate zero knowledge proofs into Automated Market Makers, offloading computation to zk coprocessors. This approach, cheaper than on-chain computations, maintains trust guarantees through on-chain proof verification. zkAMMs represent an evolution in decentralized trading platforms, enhancing efficiency while retaining the security and trust of blockchain technology. Additionally, they have the potential to offer differential privacy in transactions, a feature that enhances user privacy by adding noise to data, preventing individual data points from being distinguished. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
