/ActualText (ZK Score by Omer Shlomovits \(Ingonyama\), Lucy Williams: ZK Score is a proposed metric system for evaluating Zero Knowledge Proof \(ZKP\) technologies, focusing on efficiency at the hardware level. It measures the number of proofs generated per joule of energy consumed, providing a standardized way to compare ZK tech stacks. The goal of ZK Score is to offer a tangible, hardware-centric benchmark, akin to those in AI technologies, to assess the performance of various ZKP implementations. By measuring proofs-per-Joule, ZK Score aims to quantify the energy efficiency of ZKP systems, enabling a fair and objective comparison.  )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
