/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (On September 15th, ChainLight researchers identified a soundness bug in the ZK-circuits of the zkSync Era mainnet, promptly reporting it on the 19th. The bug permitted a malicious prover to generate false "proofs" for improperly executed blocks, which would be accepted by the L1 verifier smart contracts. Matter Labs responded by deploying a fix. The bug revolved around the handling of memory write instructions in the EraVM, allowing the alteration of transaction values.)
/E (On September 15th, ChainLight researchers identified a soundness bug in the ZK-circuits of the zkSync Era mainnet, promptly reporting it on the 19th. The bug permitted a malicious prover to generate false "proofs" for improperly executed blocks, which would be accepted by the L1 verifier smart contracts. Matter Labs responded by deploying a fix. The bug revolved around the handling of memory write instructions in the EraVM, allowing the alteration of transaction values.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
